/-!
# The small-action steps in Proposition 8.2.8

The completed cubic code exclusion uses genuine L₂(2) and nonsplit
triple-A₆ models, the canonical action on P/U, and an elementary subgroup
of order 27 lifted through the actual two-core quotient. Its application
selects D₁₀ once the finite-action alternatives have been supplied.

The finite-action sieve and the M₂₂ rank-two commutator quotient argument
are still required. Thus this interface does not yet assert all four rows
of Proposition 8.2.8(3), nor the unconditional code selection. Final
assembly remains here; the marked representation inputs belong to the
parent tensor-recognition task.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, printed pp.718–719 (PDF pp.735–736).
-/
